  "title": "API Tokens Not Revoked on Customer Password Change or Reset",
  "description": "Customer password change (changePassword) and password reset (resetPassword) clear web sessions via SessionCleaner but do NOT revoke REST API bearer tokens or JWT tokens. A stolen API token remains valid after password change.",
  "technical_details": "In AccountManagement.php, both changePasswordForCustomer() (line 1072) and resetPassword() (line 712) call $this->sessionCleaner->clearFor() but never call CustomerTokenService::revokeCustomerAccessToken(). The same issue affects GraphQL paths: ChangePassword.php (line 103-107) calls changePasswordById(), ResetPassword.php (line 115-119) calls resetPassword() — both inherit the same gap. CustomerEmailChangedObserver handles token revocation for email changes but is only registered for webapi_rest and graphql areas (not frontend). Integration\\Plugin\\Model\\CustomerUser plugin only revokes tokens on customer deactivation (is_active=0) or deletion, not credential changes. Token survival window: OAuth tokens default 1 hour (oauth/access_token_lifetime/customer=1), JWT tokens default 60 seconds (webapi/jwtauth/customer_expiration=60). The OAuth token window is the primary concern as JWT tokens expire quickly."
}

