  "id": "L-064",
  "title": "Admin API Tokens Not Revoked on Admin Password Change or Reset",
  "description": "Admin password change (via My Account) and admin password reset (via forgot password link) do not revoke admin API bearer tokens or JWT tokens. Only admin sessions are invalidated. A stolen admin API token remains valid for up to 4 hours (default OAuth lifetime).",
  "technical_details": "Admin password change path: Backend\\Controller\\Adminhtml\\System\\Account\\Save::execute() (line 78-87) sets password and calls $user->save(). The admin_user_save_after event fires, but Integration\\Plugin\\Model\\AdminUser::afterSave() only revokes tokens when is_active==0. No code in this path calls AdminTokenService::revokeAdminAccessToken(). Admin password reset path: User\\Controller\\Adminhtml\\Auth\\ResetPasswordPost::execute() (line 74-91) calls $user->save() then forceSignIn->updateAdminSessionStatus() which only updates admin_user_session status to LOGGED_OUT — this invalidates admin sessions but not API tokens. ForceSignIn helper (User\\Helper\\ForceSignIn) only calls adminSessionInfo->updateStatusByUserId(). Token survival window: OAuth admin tokens default to 4 hours (oauth/access_token_lifetime/admin=4), JWT admin tokens default to 60 seconds (webapi/jwtauth/admin_expiration=60). The explicit InvalidateToken controller (User\\Controller\\Adminhtml\\User\\InvalidateToken) does call revokeAdminAccessToken() AND forceSignIn->updateAdminSessionStatus(), showing the intended pattern that password change/reset flows fail to implement."
}

